      "title": "Numerical canonical KL bound for the actual standardized RGO",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6",
          "label": "SPHMC arXiv2609.06906v1 S2 normalized hypotheses/prox/RGO/KL; S4.Ex8 standardized posterior, FIRST S4.E6/S4.SS1.p4.3 numerical KL/Fisher ingredient.",
          "scope": "Authored sufficient actual standardizedRGO numerical canonical KL<=eta²finrank/2 intermediate for SPHMC FIRST4.6. Literal normalized globally C2/Hessian source assumptions, all positive eta and explicitly authored measurable-family/rank0 extension. Unique measurable actual prox, probability/AC/finitecanonicalKL and true smoothrho gradientL2 internally produced. Choose43p, internally use43uniqueness with31stationarity, transport every rho/Q/r output before numeric Fisher composition. No new positionmoment proof, no caller coherence/domain/law/numericbound certificate. GaussianT2/W2/FIRST4.6, fullsamplers/main/realcost/composition/reader/main/live/PURIFIED remain separate. Actual focused3827PASS; independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.StandardizedRGOKLDimension"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite complete real Hilbert/Borel E and measurable S. Finite rank zero and measurable families are explicit authored extensions; Unit recovers fixed source parameters.",
        "V is globally C2 and kappa>=1, with the exact normalized evaluated Hessian bounds kappa^-1 norm(v)^2<=D²V(x)[v,v]<=norm(v)^2 for all x,v.",
        "eta/y are measurable and eta(s)>0 at every s, without an upper restriction.",
        "Actual unique measurable p, probability/AC/finite canonical KL and true smooth-rho gradient L2 are internally produced outputs. Finite KL is retained before toReal; canonical logRN is not pointwise differentiated."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, including rank zero, and S a measurable parameter space. Let V be globally C2 with kappa>=1 and kappa^-1 norm(v)^2<=D²V(x)[v,v]<=norm(v)^2 for every x,v. For measurable eta/y with every eta(s)>0, there exists a measurable unique stationary proximal point p. Define the actual normalized volume tilt mu, its actual quadratic RGO reweighting R, its actual affine standardization r about that same p, the displayed smooth residual rho, and gamma=stdGaussian E. For every s, r(s) is a probability, absolutely continuous with respect to gamma, canonical KL is finite, gradient rho(s) is L2(r(s)), and canonical KL(r(s)||gamma).toReal<=eta(s)^2*real(finrank E)/2. No step-size upper bound, caller witness, law, coherence, domain or desired-bound certificate is assumed.",
      "formula": "D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)\\le\\frac{\\eta_s^2 d}{2},\\qquad d=\\dim_{\\mathbb R}E,\\quad\\gamma=\\mathrm{stdGaussian}(E).",
      "boundary": "Authored sufficient actual standardizedRGO numerical canonical KL<=eta²finrank/2 intermediate for SPHMC FIRST4.6. Literal normalized globally C2/Hessian source assumptions, all positive eta and explicitly authored measurable-family/rank0 extension. Unique measurable actual prox, probability/AC/finitecanonicalKL and true smoothrho gradientL2 internally produced. Choose43p, internally use43uniqueness with31stationarity, transport every rho/Q/r output before numeric Fisher composition. No new positionmoment proof, no caller coherence/domain/law/numericbound certificate. GaussianT2/W2/FIRST4.6, fullsamplers/main/realcost/composition/reader/main/live/PURIFIED remain separate. Actual focused3827PASS; independent wholeproof/blind/source/exactcommit/shared admission pending.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce the actual unique-prox law",
          "text": "The actual canonical KL/Fisher producer supplies measurable p, stationarity and uniqueness. The displayed volume tilt, quadratic reweighting and affine pushforward are the source posterior; probability, absolute continuity, finite canonical KL and the score L2 domain are actual outputs.",
          "formula": "p_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p_s)=y_s,\\quad z+\\eta_s\\nabla V(z)=y_s\\Longrightarrow z=p_s,\\quad r_s=(x\\mapsto\\eta_s^{-1/2}(x-p_s))_{\\#}\\mathrm{RGO}_{\\eta_s,y_s}.",
          "lean": "standardized_rgo_unique_prox_and_kl_le_fisher; hpm; hstat; huniq; hk"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the numerical-Fisher witness internally",
          "text": "The position/Fisher producer initially returns another stationary p prime. Uniqueness of p gives equality pointwise; Lean Core function extensionality gives equality of the families. Rewriting its entire output transports rho, Q, r, gradients and integration laws. The caller supplies no coherence condition.",
          "formula": "p'_s+\\eta_s\\nabla V(p'_s)=y_s\\Longrightarrow p'=p,\\quad(\\rho',Q',r')=(\\rho,Q,r).",
          "lean": "standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher; hstat'; huniq; Lean Core funext; rw [hp] at hd"
        },
        {
          "title": "Reuse the actual numerical Fisher estimate",
          "text": "The same-law position/Fisher parent already proves the actual second moment at most d and the score-energy bound at most eta squared times that moment. Its final output is the numerical Fisher bound below. This proof calls that genuine producer and does not repeat its moment or gradient-growth proof.",
          "formula": "I_s:=\\int\\|\\nabla\\rho_s(u)\\|^2\\,dr_s(u)\\le\\eta_s^2\\int\\|u\\|^2\\,dr_s(u)\\le\\eta_s^2 d.",
          "lean": "hd.2 s; hscoreposition; hscorebound; same literal real finrank cast"
        },
        {
          "title": "Retain canonical KL and its true domains",
          "text": "At the identical posterior and residual potential, the canonical KL/Fisher parent supplies the half-Fisher inequality together with actual probability, absolute continuity, finite canonical KL and score integrability. It is the finite canonical ENNReal KL real value, rather than a chosen density entropy or totalized infinite value.",
          "formula": "r_s\\ll\\gamma,\\quad D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)<\\infty,\\quad\\nabla\\rho_s\\in L^2(r_s),\\quad D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)\\le\\tfrac12 I_s.",
          "lean": "hk s; hprob; hac; hfin; hrho2; hkl"
        },
        {
          "title": "Compose with the exact real coefficient",
          "text": "Multiply the actual numerical Fisher inequality by nonnegative one half and use order transitivity. Exact real arithmetic gives eta squared d divided by two. No division by d, eta or energy occurs, so zero-dimensional and zero-energy cases are retained.",
          "formula": "D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)\\le\\tfrac12 I_s\\le\\tfrac12\\eta_s^2 d=\\frac{\\eta_s^2 d}{2}.",
          "lean": "mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hscorebound; norm_num; calc; ring"
        },
        {
          "title": "Exercise actual posterior consumers",
          "text": "Actual tests specialize eta=2, the positive unbounded measurable family eta(s)=s²+1 with y(s)=s v, and the zero-dimensional constant potential. The last test uses the real finrank zero upper bound and canonical KL nonnegativity to prove the actual finite KL real value is zero. T2 and the W2/FIRST step remain separate.",
          "formula": "\\eta=2;\\quad\\eta(s)=s^2+1;\\quad d=0\\Longrightarrow D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(r_s\\Vert\\gamma)=0.",
          "lean": "actual_fixed_posterior; actual_variable_step_family; rank_zero_actual_canonical_kl; finrank_euclideanSpace"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional complete real Hilbert space with its Borel structure, including rank zero, and S a measurable parameter space. Let V be globally C2 with kappa>=1 and kappa^-1 norm(v)^2<=D²V(x)[v,v]<=norm(v)^2 for every x,v. For measurable eta/y with every eta(s)>0, there exists a measurable unique stationary proximal point p. Define the actual normalized volume tilt mu, its actual quadratic RGO reweighting R, its actual affine standardization r about that same p, the displayed smooth residual rho, and gamma=stdGaussian E. For every s, r(s) is a probability, absolutely continuous with respect to gamma, canonical KL is finite, gradient rho(s) is L2(r(s)), and canonical KL(r(s)||gamma).toReal<=eta(s)^2*real(finrank E)/2. No step-size upper bound, caller witness, law, coherence, domain or desired-bound certificate is assumed.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce the actual unique-prox law; Identify the numerical-Fisher witness internally; Reuse the actual numerical Fisher estimate; Retain canonical KL and its true domains; Compose with the exact real coefficient; Exercise actual posterior consumers",
